A||N||14||Monkeyman||Another career change  ||||9||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||08-13-2001||09:23 PM||||I've decided to get back into trucking in the next month or so.  I drove in one form or another for almost 15 years, then decided about a year and a half ago to try something else (I was getting burned out) so I became a convenience store manager.  Things have been getting worse every day.  I'm to the point where I feel that driving a truck would actually be a stress reliever.  If I had any other options, I'd probably stay out of a truck, but I really need to make some money to get ahead in life and I'm only qualified to drive a truck or manage a store.  The only benefit I can think of (besides the money) is that I might be able to meet some of you.  Most of my trips will be from Indianapolis, IN to the east coast and back so maybe I can hook up with some of you in PA or thereabouts.  If I get stuck out there over a weekend, someone's getting a houseguest!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I hate changing careers again (I was kind of enjoying home life, but I actually spend more time in the store than at home) but what can I do?<P>Sorry to get long winded and rambley (yes, that's a word--sort of), but I just wanted to tell my friends about this for some reason.  Once I get back in a truck, I won't be on the forum as much but I'll bring my laptop with me and try to get on a couple times a week.  This is why I'm trying to find a relatively cheap ISP with toll free access.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||9
Z||000001||Urchin||08-13-2001||09:27 PM||||I've been considering opening my own business.  I'm not sure of what types of courses I would need to take to aqcuire the knowledge needed.  Obviously a lot of work too. Anyway, good luck with whatever you do.  Trucking or otherwise...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_3.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||annieL||08-13-2001||09:58 PM||||I work with disabled adults and that is a big time stress job. I am going to go to school in the fall for either criminal justice or elementary education. I so need a career change.<P>Good luck with your new venture!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||08-13-2001||10:24 PM||||Just a few definitions on the merits of having your own business<P>Be your own boss--- That means you do everything yourself<P>Make your own hours---you have to make about 4-5 extra hours a day, 24 just aren't enough.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-13-2001||10:32 PM||||MM,<P>Best of luck to you in your new venture!<BR>If you ever find yourself in Atlanta, give me a shout!<P>BTW... Earthlink has local dial-in numbers in LOTS of cities. Have been using Mindspring/Earthlink for years and I'm very satisfied.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Songman||08-13-2001||10:36 PM||||I've never driven a truck for a living so I can't say much about how it really is. I know that the seeming freedom of it made me dream of doing it as a child. It seems like the next best thing you can be next to a country singer if you are talking about having room for flexibility. Of course, trucking has become more and more of a business just like everything else and a lot of that freedom seems to have faded away. Of course, I never had a family to want to stay home with to so that has to play a big part.<P>Anyway, you know that all of his here wish you lots of success no matter where the road takes you. The one good side of this is that now maybe a few of us can catch up with you on number of posts! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
