Z||000007||Oreif||08-14-2001||02:45 AM||||Good Luck with the trucking. If your ever up this way let me know. Are you still planning on coming to Fierorama? Also Do you have your own truck? How about working for a trucking company that hauls cars? Maybe those who want to buy Fiero's located on the east coast can get a discount. HMM... east coast Fiero parts delivery sounds like a good business too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-14-2001||04:45 AM||||Phil (and others)--I have no intention of buying my own truck and going into business for myself.  Been there, done that.  Way too many headaches, especially in an economy like this.  <P>Raydar--Absolutely.  I'll buy the 1st round.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Songman--I'll miss my family a lot but I hope to be home most weekends.  Can't guarantee 2 full days or that the weekend will fall on a traditional Sat/Sun, but at least I'll be there.  There are some freedoms out there, but mostly it's just a job.<P>Pontiaddict--Have you ever seen "Deuce Bigalow"?  I'd end up with clients like he did!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Oreif--I'm sure I'll hit the Windy City from time to time.  As far as I know, I'll still make it to Fierorama.  I'll probably go to orientation on Monday, Sept. 17 if I can stand my current job that long.  If not, you'll just have to hand deliver my '88 GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
